    "derivation": [
      "Initial registry creates one temporary name; rename exchanges that slot for the final registry. A failed pre-rename write can retain its temp, and a post-effect rename or directory-sync failure can leave the final registry; neither branch creates a second registry name.",
      "Read-only inspection source paths are nonallocating for directory entries; alpha lock contributes one name; status/history controller lock contributes one name. Directory-open/sync handles create no entries.",
      "Cleanup failures may retain both lock names; error propagation prevents continuation/retry. Model includes explicit inspection of a visible registry after failed rename/directory-sync but does not declare installation success.",
      "Therefore max3 fits4093+3=4096. Reserve2 permits4094 then registry+two locks=4097. Info alone requires only2 but the common inspection contract includes status/history."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Model extends prior private actual-source harness to triples; independent structural/source validation supplies derivation. Exact baseline pins are checked before extraction/evaluation.",
      "Virtual native output occupancy, readonly validation and child orchestration are mocked or inspected; status/history absence of inventory means4097 is occupancy crossing, not observed command refusal.",
      "Representative failures only, not allOS/crash/concurrent/direct-controller/native/transient-fence proof.",
      "Postcreate check cannot prevent already-overbound native-created incomplete prefix.",
      "No implementation acceptance: future guard requires immutable baseline frozen BEFORE edits, candidate threshold/preservation/wiring tests and final independent integration review.",
      "Nearfull bind/apply may legitimately refuse via existing3/7; inspectability is not activation."
    ],
